From: Project Arctic
Subject: shell32: explorer's command bar takes the pictures of the menus.

The buttons of Windows 11's command bar in File Explorer (cut, copy,
paste, rename, share, delete, sort, view, new) have the same two-tone
pictures as its context menus. ArcticGetMenuPicture gives one of them for
a light or dark background at a size (menuicons.cpp).
---
diff --git a/dll/win32/shell32/shell32.spec b/dll/win32/shell32/shell32.spec
--- a/dll/win32/shell32/shell32.spec
+++ b/dll/win32/shell32/shell32.spec
@@ -666,3 +666,4 @@

 ; Arctic: the pictures of Windows 11's menus (menuicons.cpp)
 @ stdcall ArcticSetMenuIcon(ptr long long str)
+@ stdcall ArcticGetMenuPicture(str long long)
